{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q8KQL6","uniProtkbId":"PADGT_ACHLA","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2014-02-19","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2002-10-01","entryVersion":70,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Acholeplasma laidlawii","taxonId":2148,"lineage":["Bacteria","Bacillati","Mycoplasmatota","Mollicutes","Acholeplasmatales","Acholeplasmataceae","Acholeplasma"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Processive diacylglycerol alpha-glucosyltransferase"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10220338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12464611"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1533160"}],"value":"2.4.1.208"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10220338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12464611"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1533160"}],"value":"2.4.1.337"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Alpha-diglucosyldiacylglycerol synthase"},"shortNames":[{"value":"Alpha-DGS"},{"value":"DGlcDAG synthase"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Alpha-monoglucosyldiacylglycerol synthase"},"shortNames":[{"value":"Alpha-MGS"},{"value":"MGlcDAG synthase"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Glucosyl-alpha-1,2-glucosyldiacylglycerol synthase"}},{"fullName":{"value":"UDP-glucose:1,2-diacylglycerol 3-alpha-D-glucosyltransferase"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"dgs"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10220338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12464611"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1533160"}],"value":"Processive glucosyltransferase involved in the biosynthesis of both the non-bilayer-prone alpha-monoglucosyldiacylglycerol and the bilayer-forming membrane lipid alpha-diglucosyldiacylglycerol. These are major components for maintaining the anionic lipid surface charge density, for balancing the bilayer to non-bilayer phase equilibria and for keeping a constant lipid bilayer spontaneous curvature (curvature packing stress). Catalyzes the transfer of a glucosyl residue from UDP-Glc to diacylglycerol (DAG) acceptor to form the corresponding alpha-glucosyl-DAG (1,2-diacyl-3-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-sn-glycerol), which then acts as acceptor to give alpha-diglucosyl-DAG product (3-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl-alpha-(1->2)-D-glucopyranosyl)-1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol). It can only use UDP-Glc as sugar donor"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = a 1,2-diacyl-3-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-sn-glycerol + UDP + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47612"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17670"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17815"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58223"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58885"}],"ecNumber":"2.4.1.337","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10220338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12464611"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1533160"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a 1,2-diacyl-3-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-sn-glycerol + UDP-alpha-D-glucose = a 1,2-diacyl-3-O-[alpha-D-glucosyl-(1-> 2)-alpha-D-glucosyl]-sn-glycerol + UDP + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:19165"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17670"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58223"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58885"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:76166"}],"ecNumber":"2.4.1.208","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10220338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMe